  },
  "articleBody": "Wondering if it's time to give your log home a fresh new look or just some much-needed protection? It's a common question, and thankfully, there are some clear signs to look for. One of the biggest indicators is simply how your current finish is holding up. If it's starting to fail—maybe it's peeling, fading, or looking dull—that's a pretty strong signal. You definitely want to address this before widespread UV damage, checking (those little cracks in the wood), or moisture intrusion starts to progress. The key here is proactive maintenance. You don't want to wait until there are big problems to tackle. Generally, depending on how much sun and weather exposure your log home gets, reapplication of stains and clear coatings is needed every 3 to 7 years. So, if it's been a while, or if you're seeing those telltale signs of wear and tear, it's probably a good time to start thinking about an upgrade. Investing in a good finish now can save you from more costly repairs down the line. If you're in the Denver area and need some guidance, HH Remodeling LLC is here to help you assess your log home's finish and recommend the best plan of action.",
